    "Insurance is valuable because the lucky help pay for the unlucky. If the premium equals the expected cost of one's own condition, the buyer is simply paying for his own treatment in advance, so the risk is not pooled. Paragraph 3 makes the point that 'a pool sorted precisely by risk is no longer sharing much risk at all'.",
